## Summary

Declare Code Synopsis Form

## Claim

### Prose Claim

A Code Synopsis describes an Implementation’s actual code parts, behavior, and structure. It may be partial and does not require a specification. Rationale is optional; distinguish observed facts from inferred explanations and identify evidence for inferences when available. Differences from a relevant specification are neutral observations; a difference alone is not a Concern.

### Formal Claim

```CFEL
# instances
Atom/(.Header.Form := Code Synopsis)//$code_synopsis;
$code_synopsis.Header.Role:: [in (Implementation)]{::1};
$code_synopsis.Content.Claim{::1}:: []{::0};
$code_synopsis.Content.Claim.*[string, in (Formal Claim, Prose Claim)]{::1..2};
$code_synopsis.Content.Claim.Formal Claim{::0..1} :: [markdown]{::1};
$code_synopsis.Content.Claim.Prose Claim{::0..1} :: [markdown]{::1};
$code_synopsis.Content.Claim.Prose Claim ;> $code_synopsis.Content.Claim.Formal Claim
```

## Semantics

Role Implementation makes this content descriptive of actual implementation. The Claim container may contain one or both existing child Properties: Formal Claim for CFEL statements of actual facts, Prose Claim for explanation. A Formal Claim remains CFEL-fenced under the existing content contract. Code production remains governed by the applicable RMED and CA-R-1873.
